  "body": "Follow-up from #3084 (branch `issue/3084-two-rotary-first-traverse`, decision `docs/decisions/3084-posed-first-traverse.md`, \"Known limits\").\n\nThe post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the move with the rotary words (`fanuc.cps` `traverseZ`, `xyFirst`, `onRapid`). During the X/Y traverse each rotary that turns the work stands where the previous program left it.\n\n#3084 reads the multi-axis and rotary kinds through every such pose. It does not read these operations:\n\n1. A 3+2 operation (`Tilt`) on a machine with a tilting rotary that turns the work (for example the microARC 4 A, or a trunnion). The #2987 law reads the stock and the fixtures along the plane's tool axis, at the pose of the operation (`first_traverse::judge`, frame branch, `work_tilts`).\n2. A cross drill on such a machine.\n\nRisk: the first rapid can go through the stock, the part or a fixture that the previous program left turned up, and no law refuses it.\n\nWork:\n1. Read these operations with `verify::first_traverse_low_posed` (the sphere about the WCS origin for two work-turning rotaries, a full turn about the line for one), or refuse them by name.\n2. Check the shipped examples on the microARC 4 (`examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` has slot operations, not 3+2) and the index-swing tests before the change. A shipped example that changes needs the maintainer.\n3. Add pinning tests: one refused, one clear.\n\nPremise: the unknown start is at the tool-change height (maintainer decision on PR #2997).\n",
